TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  One port and two crafted client MACs.  One MAC is named in the command; the other
  never is, and is the control.  The DUT is both the authenticator and the RADIUS
  server, so no second switch and no external server took part.

        tb277  eth4   -- MAC A 02:0d:b9:00:42:77 (named in the command)
             |           MAC B 02:0d:b9:00:42:78 (the control, never named)
             |           EAPOL from tools/eapol.py, ARP from tools/arpleg.py
             |
             |  (down)  ARP requests, and EAPOL frames where a leg uses them
             |  (up)    ARP replies when the DUT allows the MAC through
             v
    +----------------------------------------------------+
    |  swi_d   AT-x960-56YSQ                   <-- DUT   |
    |  port1.0.48: dot1x port-control auto,              |
    |              dot1x control-direction both,         |
    |              auth host-mode single-host,           |
    |              auth supplicant-mac 020d.b900.4277    |
    |                       <bare | force-authorized |   |
    |                        force-unauthorized>         |
    |         |                                          |
    |         +--> radius-server local, 127.0.0.1        |
    +----------------------------------------------------+
             ^
             |  console, 115200 baud
        tb277  /dev/u2

  DUT     : swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) console u2 at 115200 baud, S/N A2WQS700B,
            software sin_x96056-20261019-27.  Not a stack.
  server  : the DUT's own local RADIUS server.  `radius-server local`, NAS 127.0.0.1,
            users ckmulti1, ckmulti2, ckpeap, cktls.  This case created no user and
            removed none.
  link    : tb277 eth4 <-> swi_d port1.0.48 (access port in vlan 48; the DUT's vlan 48
            address is 10.38.22.66/27, MAC e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43)
  clients : MAC A 02:0d:b9:00:42:77 (020d.b900.4277), sender IP 10.38.22.70.  This is
            the MAC named in every `auth supplicant-mac` command.
            MAC B 02:0d:b9:00:42:78 (020d.b900.4278), sender IP 10.38.22.71.  This is
            the control.  It is never named in any command.
  probe   : the dataplane probe is 4 ARP requests for the DUT's own vlan 48 address,
            sent to the broadcast MAC.  The measurement is how many ARP replies come
            back.  It needs no next hop and no routing, and an unauthorised port drops
            it like any other non-EAPOL frame.
  tools   : tools/eapol.py and tools/arpleg.py on tb277; tools/tb ckcon for the
            console; tools/qmark.py for the read-only help probe; tools/tb health for
            the two health reads

  Every authentication leg below was preceded by
  `dot1x initialize interface port1.0.48`.

  A note on the zeros in this log.  They are measurements, not a dead instrument.  The
  same `arpleg.py` command, changed only in its source MAC, returned 3 replies in
  STEP 2.  So the instrument is proved able to see a reply on this wire.

STEP A -- read the command surface, without running anything                 done
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: tools/qmark.py sends `?` and then Ctrl-U, so no command is executed.  Its own
  self-test was run first and passed.

awplus(config-if)# auth supplicant-mac ?
  MAC  MAC (hardware) address of the Supplicant entry in HHHH.HHHH.HHHH format

awplus(config-if)# auth supplicant-mac 020d.b900.4277 ?
  mask              MAC address mask
  max-reauth-req    No of reauthentication attempts before becoming unauthorized (default 2)
  max-req           Maximum number of times to retransmit an EAP Request packet (default 2)
  port-control      Port control commands
  quiet-period      Quiet period in the HELD state (default 60 sec)
  reauth-period     Seconds between reauthorization attempts (default 3600 sec)
  reauthentication  Enable reauthentication on a port
  server-timeout    Authentication server response timeout (default 30 sec)
  supp-timeout      Supplicant response timeout (default 30 sec)
  <cr>

awplus(config-if)# auth supplicant-mac 020d.b900.4277 port-control ?
  auto                Allow port client to negotiate authentication
  force-authorized    Force port state to authorized
  force-unauthorized  Force port state to unauthorized
  skip-second-auth    Skip second authentication

  The help text already shows the shape of the feature: an entry keyed on a MAC, which
  may carry its own copies of the port's authentication settings.  The `mask` option
  means the key can be a range.

