  => STEP 1 PASS, and it is a correction worth recording.  Naming a MAC with
     `auth supplicant-mac` creates a settings entry and changes no behaviour by itself.
     The named MAC still cannot pass traffic without authenticating.  A MAC that was
     never named still authenticates normally and is let through.  `show auth supplicant
     brief` reads `No supplicants` while the entry exists.  Anyone who reads the case
     title as "pre-authorise this MAC", or as "only this MAC may authenticate", would
     get a wrong answer in both directions from the bare command.

