  => STEP 2 PASS: the named MAC passed traffic without authenticating.  It sent zero
     EAPOL frames and still got 3 ARP replies.  The DUT says the same in its own words:
     the supplicant is listed with Mode `NONE`, status `ForceAuthorized` and no
     username, which means no authentication took place.  The counter
     `otherAuthenticationSupplicantNum` moved to 1 while
     `dot1xAuthenticationSupplicantNum` stayed 0.  The unnamed MAC, probed with the same
     instrument in the same configuration seconds later, got nothing.
     Why 3 of 4 and not 4 of 4: the first request arrived while the DUT was still
     creating the forced entry for a MAC it had not seen before, because `No supplicants`
     had been read moments earlier.  Requests 2, 3 and 4 were all answered.  The
     comparison that matters is 3 against 0, not 4 against 3, and both legs used the
     same instrument.

